	(text_box "WHERE TO FIND A SIGNAL\n\nBEAT_00..BEAT_12   generated on the unit sheets, consumed on 'RPi header'.  ~1234 Hz square, 0/3.3 V; the EDGE TIME is the measurement.\nPPS_00..PPS_11     generated on the unit sheets, consumed on 'RPi header'.  One rising edge per second.\nHELPER_FANOUT      generated on 'Helper', consumed on every unit sheet.  10.0012 MHz, 3.3 V CMOS, edges ~1-2 ns.  Skew between branches enters the measurement 1:1, so its tree is length-matched.\nHELPER_CLK         generated on 'Helper', consumed on 'RPi header' -> pin 18 (Y7, IO_L13P_T2_MRCC_13).\nI2C_SDA / I2C_SCL  header pins 3 and 5; Si5351, 8 x TMP1075, DS2482, MCP4725.  2k2 pull-ups are already fitted on the PYNQ-Z2.\n+3V3_A             front-end rail: every squarer, flip-flop, Schmitt and helper buffer.  One shared rail so threshold drift is common mode.\n+3V3_D             Si5351, TCXO and the I2C housekeeping parts only.\n+15V_HTR           heater only, from its own barrel jack; never touches the analog rails."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
